From ce8801512a3c7bdbe1cb09448dc16af9f9fdae6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:08:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Guard top-k merge reads by input-list liveness

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the promoted
series, tree ea1281f880e7535e3d87725be0156a8e38fc2fb2. This patch has no
clustered-search dependency.

Rationale: a bitwise conjunction reads WorkEntries from lists beyond the
visible extent even though their keys are then masked. Sparse candidates
with a wide planned domain expose these unwritten scratch reads under
compute-sanitizer initcheck. Guard the read with a lazy outer conditional.

Quality: selection keys, tie ordering and arithmetic on live entries are
unchanged. Inactive lists contribute the same zero key without being read.

Tests: strict initcheck exposed 4608 reads with unchanged selected outputs.
An independent original reproducer reports 1536 initcheck errors; the
fixed reproducer reports zero, with exact tie-ordered selected positions.
The guarded full snapshot gate passes initcheck, memcheck and racecheck.
Fresh patch application and patch/overlay identity pass.

Upstream status: local experimental dependency fix, not submitted upstream.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
index f5858e79cc..de1a27bcf9 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
@@ -954,11 +954,15 @@ def indexer_topk_merge_v41(
                 for i in T.serial(per):
                     j = i * threads + tx
                     c = T.min(base + j, lists * topk - 1)
+                    # List liveness must guard the global read itself. A bitwise
+                    # conjunction evaluates WorkEntries even for unwritten lists.
                     keys[j] = T.if_then_else(
-                        (j < n)
-                        & (g * fan_in + j // topk < live)
-                        & (WorkEntries[row, c] >= 0),
-                        _key16(WorkValues[row, c]),
+                        (j < n) & (g * fan_in + j // topk < live),
+                        T.if_then_else(
+                            WorkEntries[row, c] >= 0,
+                            _key16(WorkValues[row, c]),
+                            0,
+                        ),
                         0,
                     )
                 T.sync_threads()
